SUMMARY:CHS June Meeting: Working in Natives
DESCRIPTION:Cannington Horticultural Society invites you. Join us as Katherine Mathewson\, Head of the Design Program of Native Plants in Claremont\, explores the design process of incorporating native plants into your gardens with her presentation ‘Working in Natives’. \nA member of the Durham Master Gardeners\, Katherine brings her background in film and theater design to her passion for gardening. She will discuss the elements of design\, formal versus natural styles\, composition\, bloom time\, and winter interest. Additionally\, she will cover practical considerations such as watering\, weeding\, and selecting the right native plants for specific locations. \nWe look forward to Katherine’s perspective on discovering and using native plants to create a beautiful garden for your own space. \nJune Flower and Photography Show will also be presented the same evening. Entries to the Flower Show to be placed prior to 7pm. Doors open at 6:30pm. \nAll welcome – bring a friend and see what CHS is doing! \nSignup for Summer Workshops – two excellent workshop to be held in August. CHS Members receive a discount – get registered to hold your spot. \n 
URL:https://gardenontario.org/event/chs-june-meeting-working-in-natives/
LOCATION:Cannington Baptist Church\, 60 Cameron St. W.\, Cannington\, L0E 1E0
CATEGORIES:Flower & Vegetable Show,Grow With Us!,Society Meeting
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardenontario.org/wp-content/uploads/June-Meeting-poster-cropped.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Cannington Horticultural Society":MAILTO:info@canningtonhorticulturalsociety.org
GEO:44.3494655;-79.0409782
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Cannington Baptist Church 60 Cameron St. W. Cannington L0E 1E0;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=60 Cameron St. W.:geo:-79.0409782,44.3494655
END:VEVENT
