SUMMARY:CHS WORKSHOP: Garden Art with Heather
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a creative afternoon in a beautiful private garden with a guided garden tour and hands-on workshop. Inspired by nature\, Heather from ‘Blossom & Stone’ creates handcrafted cement garden art designed to bring beauty and function to outdoor spaces. \nIn this workshop\, guests will learn the basics of working with cement and create their own garden piece to take home—choose from a rhubarb-leaf bird bath\, stepping stone\, fairy door or whimsical mushroom. No experience required—just come ready to get creative and enjoy time in the garden. \nPick your project and get registered. Several different sizes for some items so reach out to us for all the details. \nPrices for items range from $30. for smaller items(fairy door\, small mushroom) up to $110. for a rhurbarb-leaf bird bath. Cannington Horticultural members receive a discounted price. \nLocation is a private garden in the Udora area. Pre-registration with payment is required to hold your spot. Due to the materials requiring time to cure\, all items will need to be picked up about one week after the workshop date. \nAugust 8\, 2026 / 10am start time.  (If workshop fills additional dates may be added) \nContact us for more details or to register: canningtonhorticulturalsociety@gmail.com \nlearn.grow.enjoy with Cannington Horticultural Society
URL:https://gardenontario.org/event/chs-workshop-garden-art-with-heather/2026-08-08/1/
LOCATION:Workshop – Private Garden\, Udora
CATEGORIES:Workshops
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardenontario.org/wp-content/uploads/Workshop-Mushroom-cement-cropped.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Cannington Horticultural Society":MAILTO:info@canningtonhorticulturalsociety.org
END:VEVENT
